        <abstract><![CDATA[<p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">One of Carlton’s earliest hotel buildings, on the corner of Leicester and Pelham Streets, 
                 the Carlton Inn and first licensed to George Edmonds (Edmunds) in 1856. At the time the Carlton Inn was built, the area north of Victoria Street, including Carlton and 
                 parts of North Melbourne, was not subject to the provisions of the </span><em style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Melbourne Building Act</em>
                 <span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> (1849). Buildings could be constructed and demolished without permits and this contributed to the somewhat 
                 haphazard development of Carlton in its early days. Later known as the Corkman Irish Pub, the building was demolished illegally over the weekend of 16 and 17 October 2016, 
                 though subject to a heritage overlay and despite a stop-work order being issued by the Melbourne City Council.</span></p><p><br /></p><p><br /></p>
                 <h1>Entries in Sands &amp; McDougall’s Melbourne and suburban directory&nbsp;</h1><p class="ql-align-justify"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: 
                 transparent;">Leicester and Pelham Streets appear under ‘North Melbourne’ in 1860 and 1865. Street numbers begin to appear on Leicester St in 1870, but Carlton Inn does 
                 not have number(s) until 1890 (digital access). It is 160-62 in 1890 and 1900, but only 160 in 1895. The stables are mentioned before the Inn and the street number(s). In December 1859, a publican’s licence was granted to John Cozens for the Carlton Inn, present occupant George Edmonds (</span><a href="http://nla.gov.au/nla.news-article5693144" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 255); background-color: transparent;"><em>Argus</em>, 7 December 1859, 3</a><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">).</span></p><p><br /></p><div class="ql-table-embed"><table style="border:none;border-collapse:collapse;"><colgroup><col width="47"><col width="66"><col width="198"><col width="132"><col width="186"></colgroup><tbody><tr style="height:0pt"><td style="border-left:solid #000000 0.5pt;border-right:solid #000000 0.5pt;border-bottom:solid #000000 0.5pt;border-top:solid #000000 0.5pt;vertical-align:top;padding:0pt 5.4pt 0pt 5.4pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;"><p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:2pt;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Libre Baskerville',serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;">1860&nbsp;</span></p></td><td style="border-left:solid #000000 0.5pt;border-right:solid #000000 0.5pt;border-bottom:solid #000000 0.5pt;border-top:solid #000000 0.5pt;vertical-align:top;padding:0pt 5.4pt 0pt 5.4pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;"><p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:2pt;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:'Libre Baskerville',serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;">p.89</span></p></td><td style="border-left:solid 